355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 157 0 R
/T (In sum, the MAV+ case documents a regional influence pathway in which European leverage is expressed less through universal rule-setting and more through institution-building, market-shaping, and networked coordination with African partners. This is an attempt to combine finance with technocratic regulatory support and coalition-based partnership, while outcomes ultimately depend on demand certainty, regulatory capability, technology transfer viability, and the coordination costs of operating across a large portfolio.)
/E (In sum, the MAV+ case documents a regional influence pathway in which European leverage is expressed less through universal rule-setting and more through institution-building, market-shaping, and networked coordination with African partners. This is an attempt to combine finance with technocratic regulatory support and coalition-based partnership, while outcomes ultimately depend on demand certainty, regulatory capability, technology transfer viability, and the coordination costs of operating across a large portfolio.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
